		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1443#p1443"><![CDATA[
I just want to also remind everyone of the first rule of this contest.<br><br>"The game must be FUN"<br><br>Club Silo has a lot of eye candy, granted. It's mechanics are very broken though.<br><br>Dogfight is great visually, and gameplay is unbreakable.<br><br>Wreck O Deck is an amazing piece of programming. My friends and I played it for hours.<br><br>Ozone Force was fun to make. I found that this competition helped me build a lot of the tools that will make a later game realized. I hope you all like it. I do.<br><br>Lisboa GTR Gasexpress is great too. The barbeque idea is so funny.<br><br><strong class="text-strong">Regarding the video</strong> it doesn't do these games justice. Club Silo's coverage doesn't even show what the real game looks like. I'm tempted to make a video of my own just to help make voting more fair. Erwin, you're kinda busy at siggraph. <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_razz.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":P" title="Razz"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=564">bmud</a> — Wed Aug 02, 2006 3:21 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
